;; fault-access-sd.expected.sexp — the expected observations for `fault-access-sd.s` (P2-SCALAR.3).
;; Validate with:
;;   python3 scripts/check_sexp_schema.py fault-access-sd.expected.sexp schema/expectations.sexp

(comment "fault-access-sd.expected.sexp — the expected observations for `fault-access-sd.s`." "" "⛔ EVERY VALUE HERE WAS DERIVED FROM THE PINNED SPECIFICATION PROSE BEFORE THE PROGRAM WAS RUN" "(EVD-05). The store access fault, cross-model: the boundary refuses the request and NOTHING is" "modified — a failing access has no effects (SEM-06, catalog C11).")
(expectations (program "fault-access-sd.s") (entry "0x80000000") (instructions 3) (step (n 0) (insn "lui x11, 0x40000") (writes (write (reg "x11") (value "0x0000000040000000"))) (derivation "0x40000 << 12 = 0x40000000; bit 31 is clear, so the sign extension adds nothing. The address is outside sail-riscv's MainMemory region, outside spike's DRAM, and no device on either platform.") (source "RVI-RV32I §1.1.4 (D-LUI-AUIPC)")) (step (n 1) (insn "addi x1, x0, 9") (writes (write (reg "x1") (value "0x0000000000000009"))) (derivation "The value that must never reach memory — materialized so a serviced store would be observable.") (source "RVI-RV32I §1.1.4")) (step (n 2) (insn "sd x1, 0, x11") (writes) (derivation "The effective address 0x40000000 is outside every declared region, so the store raises an access-fault exception at the boundary: the environment refuses the request, no memory changes (there is no memory there), and a store writes no register — the empty writes table. Measured on both references: cause 0x07, tval 0x0000000040000000 (sail's spelling: store/amo-access-fault).") (source "RVI-RV64I §3.1.3; RVI-RV32I §1.1.6 (D-ADDRESS-SPACE)")))
